<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Tiger Oats H1 headline shr rises 21 pct.</title>
<headline>Tiger Oats H1 headline shr rises 21 pct.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended March 31, 1997</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, headline (cts)   210.9	 vs  174.8</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 52.0	  vs  44.5</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   330.5	 vs  272.5</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   656.0	 vs  485.3</p>
<p>    Tax			 211.1	 vs  177.2</p>
<p>    Interest received     37.6	  vs  12.3</p>
<p>    Turnover		  7,714.1     vs  6,481.1</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts polled by Reuters had forecast EPS of 209.0, with the range 200.0-220.5, and a dividend of 53.6, with the range 52.3-54.5.  </p>
<p>Div payable July 11</p>
<p>on register June 6</p>
<p>Full name: Tiger Oats Ltd</p>
<p>    Share of associates'  8.7	   vs  2.8</p>
<p>    Abnormal items	  10.8	  vs  5.7</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482-1003</p>
</text>
